wikipedia_extract: Suzutsuki (涼月) was an Akizuki-class destroyer of the Imperial Japanese
  Navy. Her name means "Clear Moon (in Autumn)". Suzutsuki is best known for her participation
  in Operation Ten-Go as one of the battleship Yamato's eight escort ships, where
  her bow was blown off by an American torpedo. Suzutsuki survived the battle, and
  escaped American forces by reversing all the way back to port. She was used as a
  breakwater until 20 November 1945, when her name was struck from the naval register
  and she was sold for scrap soon after. Suzutsuki was the longest serving member
  of her class.
